
!PELIGRO!

This is an interim release, provided for
long-time libdisasm users to get a heads-up
on the API changes, and to provide a working
disassembler while some final features are
being polished.

The documentation and man pages are largely
OBSOLETE!

The interface is documented in the libdis.h
file.

The library and the x86dis program can be
built by typing 'make' in the top-level
directory.

Advanced make options like 'install',
'distrib', and 'uninstall' are not
supported.

The disassembler has been tested against
the instructions in ia32_test_insn.S . 
There are some at&t formatting issues due
largely to GNU as(1) working differently
from how the manual describes.

There are no known bugs in the disassembly
[aside from new features, such as implicit
operands or CPU/ISA version, being incomplete] ...
if you find a bug please report it.

